// =============================================================================
// SaaS platform Prisma fragment: InstallationMark
// =============================================================================
//
// REFERENCE SNIPPET — see 01-subscription.prisma for conventions.
//
// The identifier of the installation this database belongs to (`SC-PRIV-021`).
// A tenant's deletion erases what nobody can bring back, and it runs only where
// this row names the same identifier as the environment of the process that
// runs it: a process meant for staging, started against a restored copy of
// production's database, deletes nothing.
//
// The operator writes the row, with `<app> installation mark <identifier>`,
// and says there with `--operation test|live` how the installation operates.
// No start writes it: a developer's process started against a shared database
// right after the migration would otherwise claim that database for its own
// environment. Until somebody marks it, nothing is deleted at all.
//
// One row per installation, like `applied_settings`: the `CHECK` in
// sql/constraints.postgres.sql holds it to one row, and the default only lands
// a caller that omits the id on the right one.
//
// Required wherever tenants are served, together with fragments 29 to 31.

model InstallationMark {
    id            String   @id @default("installation")
    // As the operator typed it and the environment names it: compared exactly.
    identifier    String
    // Whether the installation is a test operation, whose documents are all
    // marked as tests. False on a mark that does not say: a test operation is
    // always the operator's deliberate step (`--operation test`).
    testOperation Boolean  @default(false)
    // When it was set, and by whom: an actor tag, as the audit log writes it.
    markedAt      DateTime
    markedBy      String

    @@map("installation_marks")
}
